        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">Chrome 150 supports <a href=\"https://webgpufundamentals.org/webgpu/lessons/webgpu-immediates.html\" rel=\"nofollow\">WebGPU immediates</a>; see <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/5199437611794432\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5199437611794432</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The web platform-facing part of this is the <code class=\"notranslate\">setImmediates()</code> method, which has already been added to BCD.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I just thought we might want to add the specific platform support notes, like all other WebGPU entries have; this PR does that.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30824",
            "title": "WebGPU setImmediates add support data",
            "date_modified": "2026-10-09T15:04:14.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-10-09T15:03:31.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "chrisdavidmills",
                "url": "https://github.com/chrisdavidmills"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Chrome added support for the CSS <code class=\"notranslate\">ruby-overhang</code> property in version 151; see <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/6560118298771456\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/6560118298771456</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The BCD is already there, although for some reason, Chrome is listed as not supporting the <code class=\"notranslate\">none</code> legacy alias of <code class=\"notranslate\">spaces</code>. I've tested it, and it does, so I'm updating the BCD in this PR.</p>\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30823",
            "title": "Chrome 151 supports ruby-overhang: none",
            "date_modified": "2026-10-09T14:01:36.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-10-09T13:07:01.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "chrisdavidmills",
                "url": "https://github.com/chrisdavidmills"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/349114?u=1185d4fc45f5ff4c4a592b30a4dd2bb5cd1b7128&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">The <a href=\"https://collector.openwebdocs.org/\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://collector.openwebdocs.org/</a> project (v10.20.15) found new features shipping in Safari Technical Preview 254 on macOS 27 which was released today. Currently, the collector covers about 90% of BCD, so the following list might not be exhaustive.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Release notes: <a href=\"https://webkit.org/blog/18420/release-notes-for-safari-technology-preview-254/\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://webkit.org/blog/18420/release-notes-for-safari-technology-preview-254/</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">New (<strong>bold</strong>) and updated keys:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>css.properties.link-parameters</li>\n<li>css.properties.link-parameters.none</li>\n<li>css.properties.list-style-type.symbols</li>\n<li>css.properties.list-style.symbols</li>\n<li>css.properties.max-lines.none (removal) (no longer in spec)</li>\n<li><strong>css.properties.max-size</strong></li>\n<li><strong>css.properties.max-size.fit-content</strong></li>\n<li><strong>css.properties.max-size.max-content</strong></li>\n<li><strong>css.properties.max-size.min-content</strong></li>\n<li><strong>css.properties.max-size.none</strong></li>\n<li><strong>css.properties.max-size.stretch</strong></li>\n<li><strong>css.properties.min-size</strong></li>\n<li><strong>css.properties.min-size.auto</strong></li>\n<li><strong>css.properties.min-size.fit-content</strong></li>\n<li><strong>css.properties.min-size.max-content</strong></li>\n<li><strong>css.properties.min-size.min-content</strong></li>\n<li><strong>css.properties.min-size.stretch</strong></li>\n<li><strong>css.types.random-item</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Notes:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>The release notes also mention border-*-radius side shorthands and interpolate-size, but I didn't see that supported yet.</li>\n<li>For wasm wide arithmetic, see <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"5776062030\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/30813\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30813/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30813\">#30813</a></li>\n</ul>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30822",
            "title": "Updates for Safari TP 254",
            "date_modified": "2026-10-09T12:31:24.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-10-09T12:23:11.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "Elchi3",
                "url": "https://github.com/Elchi3"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">…perationError</p>\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">From version 149, Chrome adds the ability for features of the <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Payment_Request_API\" rel=\"nofollow\">Payment Request API</a>/ <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Web-Based_Payment_Handler_API\" rel=\"nofollow\">Web-based Payment Handler API</a> to reject with an <code class=\"notranslate\">OperationError</code> to specifically indicate an internal error coming from the payment handler app, as opposed to user cancellation. See <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/5942637229113344\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5942637229113344</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This is now true of the <code class=\"notranslate\">PaymentRequest.show()</code> method and the <code class=\"notranslate\">PaymentRequestEvent.respondWith()</code> method.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR adds a data point for each of these.</p>\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30821",
            "title": "Add data points to indicate when Payment Handler features return an O…",
            "date_modified": "2026-10-09T11:56:34.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-10-09T11:43:58.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "chrisdavidmills",
                "url": "https://github.com/chrisdavidmills"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/349114?u=1185d4fc45f5ff4c4a592b30a4dd2bb5cd1b7128&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Firefox Nightly supports <code class=\"notranslate\">EXT_texture_norm16</code> WebGL extension</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Discovered via the OWD Collector v10.20.15.<br>\nSee <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1735401\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1735401</a></p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">None.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30816",
            "title": "Firefox Nightly supports `EXT_texture_norm16` WebGL extension",
            "date_modified": "2026-10-09T10:52:04.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-10-09T10:51:21.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "Elchi3",
                "url": "https://github.com/Elchi3"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/349114?u=1185d4fc45f5ff4c4a592b30a4dd2bb5cd1b7128&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Firefox Nightly supports wasm type reflection.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Via collector test (which gets this data point via <a href=\"https://github.com/GoogleChromeLabs/wasm-feature-detect\">https://github.com/GoogleChromeLabs/wasm-feature-detect</a>).</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">More work is needed to address <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"5319628521\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/30393\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/30393/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/30393\">#30393</a>. The Collector doesn't update the recently added and more detailed WebAssembly compat data yet.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30815",
            "title": "Firefox Nightly supports wasm type reflection",
            "date_modified": "2026-10-09T10:37:04.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-10-09T10:36:29.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "Elchi3",
                "url": "https://github.com/Elchi3"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/126397667?u=3b8d9424f1a16860e2ee3c84887049f89cbaf37c&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Adds <code class=\"notranslate\">api.console.context_static</code> for the non-standard <code class=\"notranslate\">console.context()</code> method, so the new MDN page requested in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"5746060804\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/46017\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/46017/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/46017\">mdn/content#46017</a> has compat data.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Chrome 61: the method was added in V8 commit <a class=\"commit-link\" data-hovercard-type=\"commit\" data-hovercard-url=\"https://github.com/v8/v8/commit/701d79d08ad4/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/v8/v8/commit/701d79d08ad4\">v8/v8@<tt>701d79d08ad4</tt></a> (June 2017), which is in V8 6.1 (<code class=\"notranslate\">6.1.534.32</code> contains it, <code class=\"notranslate\">6.0.286.52</code> does not). V8 6.1 shipped in Chrome 61. Confirmed present in Chrome 154.</li>\n<li>Firefox: not supported, <a href=\"https://bugzil.la/1948870\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzil.la/1948870</a> is still open.</li>\n<li>Safari: not supported, <a href=\"https://webkit.org/b/293768\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://webkit.org/b/293768</a> is still open.</li>\n<li>Deno: <code class=\"notranslate\">typeof console.context</code> is <code class=\"notranslate\">\"undefined\"</code> in Deno 2.7.5 (tracking issue <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3108971415\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/denoland/deno/issues/29560\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/denoland/deno/issues/29560/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/denoland/deno/issues/29560\">denoland/deno#29560</a>).</li>\n<li>Node.js 8.7.0: first release with V8 6.1 (<code class=\"notranslate\">deps/v8/include/v8-version.h</code>), and its <code class=\"notranslate\">lib/internal/bootstrap_node.js</code> already copies V8-only console methods onto the Node.js console. Marked as partial because messages are only sent to an attached inspector (<a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"2794011602\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/nodejs/node/issues/56634\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/nodejs/node/issues/56634/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/nodejs/node/issues/56634\">nodejs/node#56634</a>). I confirmed that behavior in Node.js 22.14 using <code class=\"notranslate\">inspector.Session</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">Runtime.consoleAPICalled</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><code class=\"notranslate\">npm run lint</code> passes apart from the expected 404 warning for the <code class=\"notranslate\">mdn_url</code>, which the mdn/content PR adds.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Relates to <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"5746060804\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/46017\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/46017/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/46017\">mdn/content#46017</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30814",
            "title": "Add `console.context()` static method",
            "date_modified": "2026-10-09T09:42:36.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-10-09T09:41:50.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "agnij-dutta",
                "url": "https://github.com/agnij-dutta"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/349114?u=1185d4fc45f5ff4c4a592b30a4dd2bb5cd1b7128&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Add an entry for the wide arithmetic wasm proposal.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Via collector test (which gets this data point via <a href=\"https://github.com/GoogleChromeLabs/wasm-feature-detect\">https://github.com/GoogleChromeLabs/wasm-feature-detect</a>).</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This was missed in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"5248033996\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/30327\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30327/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30327\">#30327</a></p>",
